      "extract": "It is possible to get numerical results by using linear programming to ﬁnd functions for use in Theorem 3.1, as was done for the kissing problem by Odlyzko and Sloane in [OS]. The idea is to ﬁx one of f(0) and bf(0), and view extremizing the other as an inﬁnite-dimensional linear programming problem. One can try to approximate it with a ﬁnite-dimensional problem, and solve it on a computer. Although we obtained some",
