      "extract": "It is natural to ask whether the densest sphere packing in Rn is unique. Of course, it is trivially not unique, since for example removing a single sphere does not change the global density. However, it is conjectured that E8 and the Leech lattice are unique among periodic packings. By contrast, in R3 there are inﬁnitely many distinct periodic packings of maximal density. Our techniques can be used to prove this",
