      "extract": "In this appendix, we provide precise statements and references for what it means for a packing to have a density and whether there is a maximally dense packing. Much of our discussion closely follows Section I of [K]. Let P be any sphere packing in Rn. We say that P has density ∆if for all p ∈Rn, we have ∆= lim r→∞ vol(B(p, r) ∩P) vol B(p, r) , where B(p, r) is the ball of radius r centered at p, and B(p, r) ∩P",
